# Git workflow

## Branches
- `main` — production. Protected. No direct development. No agent commits or pushes.
- `test` — integration / QA. Feature work merges here first.
- `release/<rel-id>` — cut from `test` for a release. Merged into `main` only
  by human approval.
- `feature/<feature-id>-<description>` — implementation **only after `PLANNED`**
- `bugfix/<bug-id>-<description>` — fixes
- `docs/<description>` — documentation only
- `chore/<description>` — maintenance

Work only on a feature/bugfix/docs/chore/release branch. Never commit on `main`.

## Pull requests
- Implementation PRs target `test`
- Release PRs are `release/<rel-id>` → `main` and require human merge
- Do not merge PRs to `main`
- Do not approve your own human-required gates

## Release merges
After a human merges `release/<rel-id>` → `main`, the agent:
1. Merges `release/<rel-id>` → `test`, so `main` and `test` match.
2. Deletes `release/<rel-id>` — only if that merge succeeded.

If the merge into `test` fails, stop. Don't force it, don't delete the
branch. Flag it for the human.

## Commits
Conventional Commits with work item ID when present:
feat(AUTH-001): implement user login
test(AUTH-001): add login e2e tests
fix(AUTH-001): handle invalid credentials
docs(AUTH-001): add login test plan

## Push
Push only when the human asks to push or prepare/update a PR. Never push to
`main`. Exception: the test-sync merge and branch deletion in "Release
merges" — those happen automatically, no separate push request needed.
